1 NOTE {geni:about_me} IV. The Swedish Mackays, now von Key 
2 CONT
2 CONT These Mackays settled in Sweden in the time of the 1st Lord Reay  [ [http://www.geni.com/people/Donald-Mackay/6000000020799512903 Donald Mackay], 1st Lord Reay (1614-1650) , fiar of Strathnaver], and came thither as members of the
2 CONC  Scots regiment which he raised for service under Gustavus Adolphus. " With the regiment were several officers of the name of Mackay," says the Svensk Slaktbok, " who accompanied it to Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Among those coming in with the said regiment were the under named  James Mackay. and a Rudolph Mackay, whose son Isaac [corrupt form of lye] became proprietor of an ironwork in Gestrickland and married Anna Lenfstadius in 1647. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This family has signed itself Mackay, Mackey, etc., but now calls itself von Key."
2 CONT
2 CONT The family settled in Gothland in the south-east corner of Sweden, and chiefly in the counties of Kalmar and Jonkoping. Our authority for the following account is  wholly the Svensk Slaktbok, published in Stockholm by P. A. Norste
2 CONC dt, 1901
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 343
2 CONT
2 CONT   THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews  University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH :  NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY,  ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI 
