0 @N6000000002577017195@ NOTE !SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- 18 Aug 1993: Data is from the records of Owen B Anderson.
1 CONT 2- Notes on this record says that the data came from Swedish Histories C;  p 171. These are may be found in the Family History Library in SLC, UT.
1 CONT 3- Swedish Postal Address Book; Stake Family History Center.
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1- Some of this family has the parish name of Berg, Kronoberg county. This is a good place to start our research.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- 1996:The locality spelled "Oijchult" is not listed in the postal  book. There is a village spelled "Öjhult" in Göteryd Parish, Jönköping  county. Also an address Öjhult, S. Mo (Valdshult), Jönköping.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- THe locality spelled "Elkeryds" is not listed in the postal book either. There these addresses listed in the Swedish postal book:
1 CONT Ekeryd-gd, Bankeryd parish, Jönköping, Sweden
1 CONT Ekeryd-gd:ar, (army barracks) Femsjo, Jönkjöping, Sweden
1 CONT Ekeryd-gd (small village), Jönköping, JKP, Sweden
1 CONT Ekeryd-gd, Flisby, Jönköping, Sweden
1 CONT I am going to use the first placename of "Ojhult" in the birth place field and consider the village of Ekeryd in the parish and county of Jönköping, Sweden.
